# SDD Core — Spec-Driven Development Rules

## When triggered
- User asks to implement something WITHOUT referencing a spec
- User says "faz", "implementa", "cria", "código", "code", "feature"
- User mentions "spec" or "especificação"

## Mandatory workflow

```
1. VERIFY: Does a spec exist in specs/ for this feature?
   ├── YES → Read the spec, use it as source of truth
   └── NO  → STOP. Ask user: "Quer criar uma spec primeiro?"
   
2. GENERATE: Based on the spec
   - Follow types and interfaces EXACTLY
   - Implement ALL business rules
   - Handle ALL error scenarios
   
3. VALIDATE: Check that code matches spec
   - Types match
   - Rules implemented
   - All scenarios covered
```

## Anti-patterns to BLOCK
| Anti-pattern | Block it by |
|-------------|-------------|
| Generate code without spec | Refuse: "SDD requires a spec first" |
| Add fields not in spec | Refuse: "Not in spec" |
| Ignore business rules | Refuse: "Spec says otherwise" |
| Skip validation | Always validate against spec |
